## Citations

Every fact ends with a footnote whose target is an evidence sidecar `{{ paths.evidence }}` showing the exact page, paragraph, slide, transcript cue or table rows of the original document. Always cite the footnote target. Prefer citations marked `✓ quote verified` or `table`; treat `OCR` with care and never cite a `generated description` as a quote. Keep quotes in the original language of the document.

## Contradictions and superseded information

Prefer current sources over superseded ones and say so. When current sources disagree, show both claims with their citations, authority and dates, and state the resolution rule of this wiki ({{ resolution_order | join(", then ") }}) instead of silently applying it.

